    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-s/q7",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-s/q7-question-1.svg\" alt=\"The events A and B are such so that P ( A ∪ B′ ) = 0.92 ,    ( P A ′∪ B ) = 0.5 and    ( P A ′ ∪ B ′ ) = 0.88 . ( 10 ) Determine the value of ( P A ′ ∩ B ′ ) .\" style=\"--madas-width:576.0px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-s/q7-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Looking at the same Venn diagram: Taking complements gives P(A′ ∩B) = 0.08, [B1] [A1] P(A ∩B′) = 0.50 [M1] [A1] and P(A ∩B) = 0.12. [M1] [A1] These three regions and A′ ∩B′ partition the sample space: [M1] [A1] The remaining probability is 1 −0.08 −0.50 −0.12 = 0.30 . [M1] [A1] Alternative working. Label the four regions x, y, z, w, respectively, for A only, both events, B only and neither:\" style=\"--madas-width:680.0px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-s/q7-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Summing the regions in each given union gives x + y + w = 0.92, w + y + z = 0.50, x + z + w = 0.88. Since x + y + z + w = 1, the first two give z = 0.08 and x = 0.50. Alternatively sum the three union equations: 2(x + y + z) + 3w = 2.30. Since x + y + z = 1 −w, this reads 2 + w = 2.30. The third then gives w = 0.88 −0.50 −0.08 . = 0.30\" style=\"--madas-width:540.0px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 7 is 10 marks.</p>"
    ],
