    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-s/q10",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-s/q10-question-1.svg\" alt=\"Relative to a fixed origin O , the horizontal unit vectors i and j are pointing due east and due north, respectively. A particle P is moving from point A to point B , with constant acceleration of ms− 2 ( p i + q j ) , where p and q are constants. The velocity of P at A is ms− and the velocity of P at B is ( ms−. ( i − j ) 1 i + j ) 1 10 13 22 22 ms−, find the value of p and the 2 Given that the magnitude of the acceleration is 3.7 value of q . ( ) 9\" style=\"--madas-width:566.7px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-s/q10-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"The velocity changes by 12i + 35j in m s−1, with magnitude 37 m s−1. [B1] [A1] Since the acceleration is constant, this change over time ∆t is a∆t. [M1] [A1] Equating components gives p∆t = 12, q∆t = 35. Squaring and adding gives (p2 + q2)(∆t)2 = 144 + 1225 . = 1369 Since p2 + q2 = 3.72, use the positive square root. Thus ∆t = 37/3.7 = 10 s, [M1] [A1] which gives p = 1.2, q = 3.5 . [M1] [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
