      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-s/q13-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Both halves have length 39 cm, and both endpoints are at the same height: [M1] Hence each makes the same angle α with the horizontal: [A1] If the particle has mass m, balance on the particle gives T sin α = mg/2. [A1] For each ring the wire’s normal reaction is R = mg/3 + mg/2 , [A1] = 5mg/6 and the horizontal pull T cos α is balanced by friction of magnitude at most R/4 = 5mg/24. [A1] Thus cot α = T cos α/(T sin α) ≤5/12, [A1] so cos α ≤5/13. [A1] At the limiting separation cot α = 5/12, giving a 5-12-13 triangle and horizontal projection 39(5/13) = 15 cm on each side: The separation AB = 2(39) cos α [M1] is therefore at most 30 cm . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 13 is 10 marks.</p>"
