    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-s/q14-question-1.svg\" alt=\"Two cars, A and B , are travelling on a straight horizontal road. ms−, 1 At time t = 0 , A drives past a fixed point O on the road with speed 4.95 ms−. 2 accelerating uniformly at 2 After passing through O , A continues accelerating for 4 s , reaching a speed which it maintains thereafter. ms−, until it 2 At time t = 2 , B starts from rest from O ,  accelerating uniformly at 1.5 reaches the point P , where it draws level with A . ( 10 ) Determine the distance OP .\" style=\"--madas-width:577.3px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-s/q14-question-2.svg\" alt=\"Question diagram\" style=\"--madas-width:573.3px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-s/q14-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Worked solution diagram\" style=\"--madas-width:566.7px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-s/q14-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"At t = 4, A has speed 4.95 + 2(4) = 12.95 m s−1 [B1] [A1] and displacement 4.95(4) + (4)2 = 35.8 m. [A1] On 2 ≤t ≤4, [A1] A starts ahead and its speed is greater than B’s, so the meeting is later: [A1] For t ≥4 equate the displacements: 35.8 + 12.95(t −4) = 0.75(t −2)2, 0.75t2 −15.95t + 19 = 0. [M1] [A1] Multiply by 20 to obtain 15t2 −319t + 380 = 0. Factor as (t −20)(15t −19) = 0. The earlier root would fall before B starts: The roots are 20 and 19/15, of which only 20 is in the relevant interval. [A1] Thus OP = 0.75(20 −2)2 = 243 m . [M1] [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:678.7px\"></figure>",
      "<p class=\"madas-total\">Total mark for question 14 is 10 marks.</p>"
