    "id": "madas/alevel-applied-s/q16",
    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-s/q16-question-1.svg\" alt=\"A 185 N 60 N B D 63 N 84 N C\" style=\"--madas-width:434.7px\"></figure><figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-s/q16-question-2.svg\" alt=\"∡ The figure above shows a light rigid framework ABCD , where BDA = 90 ° and ∡ BCD = 90 ° . It is also given that AB = 0.37 m , BC = 0.28 m , CD = 0.21 m and AD = 0.12 m . Forces of magnitude 185 N , 84 N , 63 N and 60 N are acting along AB , BC , CD and AD , in the directions indicated by the arrows in the figure. The 4 forces reduce to a single force acting at some point P on AD , and at right angles to AD . ( ) Determine the distance AP . 8\" style=\"--madas-width:573.3px\"></figure>",
    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-s/q16-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Worked solution diagram\" style=\"--madas-width:605.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-s/q16-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"Pythagoras in ABD gives BD = 0.35 m. [B1] Resolve horizontally to the right and vertically upwards: [M1] The force 185 N along BA has components (175, 60), and the 60 N force has components (0, −60). The lower triangle is a 3-4-5 triangle. [A1] Its forces along BC and CD have components respectively 84(4/5, −3/5) = (67.2, −50.4), 63(3/5, 4/5) = (37.8, 50.4). [A1] The sums are 175 + 67.2 + 37.8 = 280 horizontally and 60 −60 −50.4 + 50.4 = 0 vertically: Their resultant with the first two forces is 280 N to the right: [A1] The source combines the forces in pairs using similar triangles: The upper pair has scale factor 500: 0.37(500) = 185, 0.12(500) = 60, leaving a horizontal resultant 0.35(500) = 175 N through A. The lower pair has factor 300: 0.28(300) = 84, 0.21(300) = 63, leaving 0.35(300) = 105 N horizontally through C. Let E be the projection of C onto the vertical through A, D.\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-s/q16-solution-3.svg\" alt=\"Equating the two expressions for the area of triangle BCD gives 1 2(0.28)(0.21) = 1 2(0.35)DE, DE = 0.168, AE = 0.12 + 0.168 = 0.288. The parallel forces divide their separation in the inverse ratio 105 : 175 = 3 : 5, so AP = (3/8)(0.288) = 0.108 m. The same result follows from the component moments: Taking anticlockwise moments about A, the BA and AD forces have zero moment. [M1] Using position vectors (−.35, −.12) for B and (0, −.12) for D, the net moment is (−.35)(−50.4) −(−.12)(67.2) −(−.12)(37.8) = 30.24 N m. [A1] The moment contributions are 17.64 + 8.064 + 4.536 = 30.24.\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-applied-s/q16-solution-4.svg\" alt=\"Dividing this moment by the horizontal resultant gives the perpendicular distance from A. The equivalent force has moment 280 AP, so AP = 0.108 m . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:677.3px\"></figure>",
